  "notes": [
    "Tower and USB base coupon were freshly sliced. Mascot, eyes, rear cover, one-screw LED retainer and USB cover coupon retain exact SHA-identical slice/component-check evidence; their records are unchanged.",
    "The long integral cover pushers are removed. A flat LED retainer carries three short flange pads and a rigid upper tab engaging the tower roof pocket; one lower screw secures it. It is a sliding rigid tab, not a flexible snap. Retainer bounds are 7.1 x 26.6 x 3.75 mm; print the rear screw-head face on the bed.",
    "Retainer plate thickness is 3.0 mm. Upper tab engagement is 1.0 mm, nominal pocket clearance 0.25 mm, and release drop 1.3 mm. The retainer and pad edges have 0.15 mm chamfers. Rear cover returns to 24 x 45.5 x 2.4 mm.",
    "The measured 8.5 mm total plastic LED length includes its 1.2 mm flange, giving a 7.3 mm barrel. Seats remain at Y=3.8 mm, giving 3.25\u20133.50 mm dome projection with 0.25 mm axial play. Tower collars extend 1.4 mm beyond the 2.4 mm front wall.",
    "LED centers remain Z=27.0, 33.5 and 40.0 mm at 6.5 mm pitch. Measured barrel diameter stays 4.75 mm, bores stay 5.1 mm, and 0.4 mm entry lead-ins leave 0.6 mm between adjacent mouths.",
    "Tower export stays 24 x 45.5 x 25 mm with a 14 mm-wide upright. Mascot remains 47.3 x 35.75 x 20.5 mm; one eye is 3.25 x 6.5 x 2.6975 mm, quantity two. Screw pilots are 1.9 mm and hand locating pin/socket sizes are 3.0/3.3 mm.",
    "Integral PCB side rails have a 45-degree top haunch back to the base walls. The 0.25 mm rear entry chamfer is limited to the three C-slot mouth edges per rail, retaining material at the rail/wall/floor roots through the rear seam. Two short C-section returns capture the non-USB end corners, each 2.5 mm wide with nominal 0.60 mm PCB overlap, 0.15 mm entry chamfer and 0.10 mm top clearance; the middle 13 mm stays open. PCB bottom remains Z=2.8 mm over the 2.0 mm floor. USB throat is unchanged at 9.15 x 3.20 mm, Z=5.25 mm, with 0.15 mm corner bevels and 0.20 mm entry chamfers on both sides.",
    "Far-end corner capture assumes component-free corner patches. The provisional top-component envelope excludes a 2.7 mm-wide by 1.0 mm-deep patch at each non-USB corner; these patches are not measured hardware clearance or physical fit validation.",
    "All seven current meshes passed actual-extrusion component checks and sampled layer connectivity. No entirely missing components or sampled isolated layer starts were found. These checks do not establish full local support, strength or hardware fit.",
    "All current slices returned Success with code 0. No geometry, support, repair, floating-region or nonroutine algorithm diagnostics were reported. Historical USB-cover ZFiller is absent from current evidence.",
    "Slicer arrangement can rotate parts in the bed plane. Extrusion checks resolve 0/90/180/270-degree XY rotation against first-layer extrusion. Partial top layers are sampled inside remaining material with STL floating-point tolerance in layer counting.",
    "Main assembly has five unique files and six physical pieces including two eyes; USB test adds two coupon pieces. Separate-copy estimates include startup and purge; grouped-plate estimates differ.",
    "Physical coupon choices remain hardware dimension references. Earlier tray-based fit feedback does not validate the compact assembly, integrated PCB guides, deeper LED seats or current retainer and corner captures; physical fit remains unverified.",
    "No G-code is delivered. Bambu PETG Basic brand/profile and Textured PEI validation plate are explicit assumptions; retain the established settings and plate used for successful physical coupons."
  ],
